# What the Archipelago 0.6.7 worker image is built from. The file name is the base: the build
# fails if BASE_COMMIT reports a different Utils.__version__.
#
# BASE_COMMIT is a commit of https://github.com/ionium-ap/Archipelago.git, and the tag beside it
# names the same commit. Those tags never move. A new patch on the 0.6.7 line gets the next tag
# (0.6.7-ionium.2) and this pin moves to it.

# 0.6.7-ionium.1
BASE_COMMIT=f04b3a3457efbca6fde29beaf70c7f7f0016cdc8

# https://github.com/ionium-ap/Archipelago-fuzzer.git
# The workers don't use the fuzzer, only index CI does, and index CI depends on what this commit
# has: `--stall-timeout`, which makes a run give up when a generation never reports back (it
# used to wait until the job's own six-hour limit, and lose its report), exit code 3 for such
# a run, and `stats.unfinished` in report.json. The hooks in index CI's checker image are the
# ones of this commit and no others. Both bases pin the same commit.
FUZZER_COMMIT=eef8c8034735d129f48457768479b1726e59be3e

# https://github.com/ionium-ap/aplinter
LINTER_COMMIT=52cfa67f7e40ebe15bf6bff6d17adb6409ad97dc
